f 17592186280294 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281160 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186280586 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281160 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281160 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281160 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186280179 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281160 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "b9a1c281-1dcb-592f-8bb1-786e3c4e7bdc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281175 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186278629 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281175 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186278665 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281175 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186278735 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281175 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186280278 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281175 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186280818 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281175 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281175 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281175 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186278665 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281175 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "c42f751a-ec9a-5f92-8bd2-846f2ed3dd93" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281543 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186281175 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281543 #edb/ref 1069 "q-162780" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281543 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281543 #edb/ref 1071 "Use the method of Lagrange multipliers to find the minimum value of the function $f(x,y)={x}^{2}-8{y}^{2}$ given that ${x}^{2}+5{y}^{2}\\le 25.$ \n\n*Hint: The critical point of $f(x,y)$ in the region ${x}^{2}+5{y}^{2}<25$ is $(0,0).$*" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281543 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e45729b0-5cc3-5497-8a8a-a3af06f9f95a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281543 #edb/ref 1074 "We are given that the critical point of $f(x,y)$ in the region's interior is $(0,0).$\n\nNext, we need to find the minimum value of $f(x,y)$ subject to the constraint $g(x,y)={x}^{2}+5{y}^{2}=25.$ \n\nSince $f(x,y)$ is continuous and the constraint is closed and bounded, $f(x,y)$ reaches a global maximum and a global minimum on the constraint. \n\nTherefore, by the method of Lagrange multipliers, we must solve the following system:\n\n$$\n∇f(x,y)=\\lambda ∇g(x,y),\\,g(x,y)=25\n$$\n\nWe start by solving the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & =\\lambda ∇g(x,y,) \\\\ ⟨{f}_{x}(x,y),{f}_{y}(x,y)⟩ & =\\lambda ⟨{g}_{x}(x,y),{g}_{y}(x,y)⟩ \\\\ ⟨2x,-16y⟩ & =\\lambda ⟨2x,10y⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x &=2\\lambda x \\\\ -16y &=10\\lambda y\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,⇒\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x(1-\\lambda ) &=0 \\\\ -2y(8+5\\lambda ) &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve this system, we break it up into several cases:\n\n- Assuming $x=0$ in the first equation of the system, the constraint condition $g(x,y)=25$ implies\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{y}^{2} & =25\\,⇒\\,y=\\pm \\sqrt{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives the critical point $(0,\\pm \\sqrt{5}).$\n\n- Assuming $y=0$ in the second equation of the system, the constraint condition $g(x,y)=25$ implies\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & =25\\,⇒\\,x=\\pm 5,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives the critical point $(\\pm 5,0).$\n\nTherefore, $f$ has possible extreme values at the points\n\n$$\n(0,\\pm \\sqrt{5}),\\,(5,0),\\,(0,0).\n$$\n\nWe evaluate $f$ at each of these points. These are given in the following table:\n\n| $(x,y)$ | $(0,\\pm \\sqrt{5})$ | $(\\pm 5,0)$ | $(0,0)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,f(x,y)\\,$ | $-40$ | $25$ | $0$ |\n\nTherefore, the function reaches a minimum value at $(0,\\pm \\sqrt{5}),$ and its minimum value is $-40.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186360926 #edb/ref 1080 "54\\,\\text{in}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360926 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360926 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1609399a-f596-5865-ab9c-6aadc92d23db" #edb/ref 